    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="1010" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-05T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1928—7
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>56. Referring to previous communications regarding the proposed Austrian
                    loan:</p>
                <p>The Department is informed confidentially that the European Governments which
                    hold relief bonds are making the subordination <pb facs="1011" n="883"
                        xml:id="pg883"/> of lien in favor of the new loan conditional upon agreement
                    by Austria to settle definitely the relief credits. The Department’s
                    understanding was that these Governments were in principle agreeable to
                    subordination of lien if all Governments similarly situated took like action and
                    if the Reparation Commission allowed suitable release. Mr. Leith Ross, of the
                    British Treasury, on December 12, 1927, so informed the Austrian Minister in
                    London (see the Reparation Commission’s Annex 3271–J).<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d736-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Department would welcome any discreetly available information as to the
                    report above as well as with regard to the status of negotiations on the relief
                    debt.</p>
                <p>Please cable your reply and repeat it to the Legation in Austria.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
